# The measured tables are pinned by SHA-256 in mspine/tables/PROVENANCE.md and
# checked on load. Git's CRLF normalisation therefore has to be switched off for
# them: with core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout stored LF in the blob while the
# pinned digest named the CRLF bytes, so the same commit verified on Windows and
# failed on Linux with a hash mismatch. A digest that depends on which machine
# cloned it is not a digest.
#
# This is not hypothetical -- it is the failure the first CI run reported:
#   ccpp/ccpp.csv hash mismatch: 76855630... != 79e1c452...
mspine/tables/**/*.csv   -text
mspine/tables/**/*.txt   -text
LICENSE-kinetics-spine   -text
